ision, attention, responsibility, but crew cooperation issues. A has decision and technical, but lacks stress and reliability.\n\nThus B seems balanced: reliability, stress, technical. Crew cooperation issue is pretentious and wrong tone, but could be mitigated. C's crew cooperation is good but decision quality is good, but lack stress resilience is concerning for long flights. D's crew cooperation is poor. A's reliability unknown.\n\nThus I might argue that B remains best overall, despite Agent 1's concerns. I can respond by saying I still think B is best, because stress resilience and reliability are paramount, and while crew cooperation issues exist, they are comparable to others. Provide evidence: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at weather, computer skills. Compare to C's lack of stress resilience evidence. So I will keep recommendation for B.\n\nThus my public message: I acknowledge Agent 1's points, but I argue B still stronger. Provide evidence. Then metadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nLet's craft."}
